  "description": "Reid Quest 1 SO eBike | Electric bike\nComfortable, capable and ready for new routes – an electric bike built for everyday journeys, weekend rides and light trail adventures.\nThe Reid Quest 1 SO eBike combines practical features with smooth electric assistance, making it a versatile choice for commuting, recreational cycling and exploring a variety of routes.\nIts lightweight alloy frame features internal cable routing and an integrated 36V 374Wh battery for a clean, streamlined finish. An 80mm suspension fork helps absorb bumps and vibrations, adding comfort across uneven roads, cycle paths and light off-road terrain.\nPowered by an Ananda 250W hub motor, the Quest 1 SO provides steady electric assistance to help with hills and longer distances. The Ananda D19 handlebar-mounted display keeps essential ride information within easy reach and offers Bluetooth connectivity and app compatibility.\nAn L-TWOO 7-speed trigger shifter works alongside a Shimano rear derailleur and 14-28T freewheel to provide straightforward gearing for different riding conditions. Tektro hydraulic disc brakes offer dependable stopping power, while Kenda 27.5 x 2.35-inch tyres deliver grip, stability and comfort across varied surfaces.\nDesigned with rider comfort in mind, the bike also features 700mm alloy riser handlebars, an adjustable 80mm stem, a plush Comfort Plus saddle and ergonomic lock-on grips for a relaxed riding position.\nThe Quest 1 SO eBike is ideal for:\n\nEveryday commuting, with electric assistance to make regular journeys easier\n\nLeisure and weekend cycling, offering a comfortable ride for exploring further afield\n\nLight off-road riding, with an 80mm suspension fork and grippy Kenda tyres\n\nHilly routes and longer distances, supported by a 250W rear hub motor and 374Wh battery\n\nComfort-focused riders, with riser handlebars, an adjustable stem and ergonomic finishing touches\n\nRiders wanting reliable control, with Tektro hydraulic disc brakes and versatile 7-speed gearing\n\nPlease make sure to familiarise yourself with eBike safety information before charging or using your new Reid. You can view and download user manuals and safety instructions here.",
